    Stereo frames on a Wayland subsurface
 
    The two views of a stereo frame go to the compositor side by side,
-   left view first, each at full size, on a subsurface of the display
-   widget's window, with a viewport that gives it the size of one view.
-   The subsurface is declared once as full side by side through
-   libstereo-declare (KWin's stereo content protocol); it takes no input,
-   which goes to the widget below it.
+   left view first, each at the resolution the frame carries it at, on a
+   subsurface of the display widget's window, with a viewport that gives
+   it the size one view is shown at.  The views are copied, never scaled:
+   a top-and-bottom 1920x1080 frame becomes one 3840x540 buffer, a side
+   by side (half) one two 960x1080 views, and the compositor resizes them
+   once to the viewport.  The subsurface is declared once as full side by
+   side through libstereo-declare (KWin's stereo content protocol); it
+   takes no input, which goes to the widget below it.
 
